# Apollo Router keys its query-plan caches on a digest of the *projection* the
# traversal visits. `QueryHashVisitor` (SHA-256) walks the executable document
# and hashes field names, parent type names, argument names and values, visited
# types and fragments -- deliberately normalized so formatting and aliases do
# not change the key. Two genuinely different operations can project to the
# same visited fields. `CachingQueryKey`'s Display, the key the in-memory and
# Redis plan caches share, mixes that QueryHash with the operation name, cache
# metadata and plan options -- never the serialized operation text and never
# the schema. With distributed query-plan caching over Redis, an operation
# could retrieve and run the plan cached for a different operation. The v1.45.1
# release commit ff9f666598cd17661880fe7fc6e9c9611316e529 bundles the fix: it
# folds `executable.to_string()` into the digest inside `hash_query`, threads
# the raw schema string through the visitor and hashes it whole when an
# introspection field (`__schema` / `__type`) is met, and adds the schema SDL
# to `CachingQueryKey`'s Display.
#
# Nothing separates the two revisions. On the subtree the fix touches
# (apollo-router/src/spec/query + apollo-router/src/query_planner, materialized
# clean from each revision), three `--cache off` runs per side (timeout 180,
# --max-ram 6GB) report 14 findings and 43 flags at both revisions, identical
# except three line-number shifts where the fix inserted lines. No finding or
# flag sits on the digest path at either revision. `vyql match` labels
# hash_query's parameters `code.ExternalEntryInput` and nothing hash-shaped;
# `vyql trace` shows the executable parameter's taint reaching
# `traverse.document` and `Ok` in the same body and stopping there as external
# calls -- the document does reach the digest calls, so this is not a flow the
# engine mishandles (the Rust return-flow gap does not apply: no hop crosses a
# function return). What is wrong is how much of the input the digest covers,
# and that is a property of the projection, not of any call.
#
# The one hash-shaped finding in the file, VYQL-CRY-001 (`code.WeakHash`), sits
# on `stats_report_key_hash`'s SHA-1 -- a different function with a different
# weakness, present unchanged at both revisions, firing identically at
# caching_query_planner.rs:516 (parent) and :519 (fix). The last case pins
# that: the nearest detection is revision-blind and off-target.
#
# No fix is justifiable today. The sole intra-procedural discriminator between
# the revisions is the fix's own added statement,
# `executable.to_string().hash(&mut visitor)`, plus the threaded schema folds;
# a binding keyed on its absence keys on the fixing commit's own layout, and
# folding text into a digest has unbounded correct spellings, so the negation
# flags every correct implementation that incorporates its input differently.
# The property itself -- a cache key's digest omits an input the cached
# artifact depends on -- is a sufficiency judgement no binding can read from an
# API's documentation, and minting a concept for it is one per weakness
# instance rather than per weakness class. The nearest existing concepts each
# assume a different weakness: `code.WeakHash` judges the algorithm (SHA-256
# here), `code.NamespacedSubjectKeyCollision` a Kubernetes reflector cache,
# `code.PublicVisibilityCacheInvalidationMissing` sandbox-proxy status entries,
# `code.SessionHashMissingAuthorizationState` session hashes over passwords.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap

test "rank1687: hash_query digests only the visited projection of the operation, so distinct operations sharing visited fields collide in the plan-cache key"
  lang rust
  file apollo-router/src/spec/query/change.rs
  reject VYQL-CRY-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-036
  reject VYQL-AUTH-058
  code
  ```
  impl<'a> QueryHashVisitor<'a> {
      pub(crate) fn hash_query(
          schema: &'a schema::Schema,
          executable: &'a executable::ExecutableDocument,
          operation_name: Option<&str>,
      ) -> Result<Vec<u8>, BoxError> {
          let mut visitor = QueryHashVisitor::new(schema, executable);
          traverse::document(&mut visitor, executable, operation_name)?;
          Ok(visitor.finish())
      }

      pub(crate) fn finish(self) -> Vec<u8> {
          self.hasher.finalize().as_slice().into()
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1687: the fixed revision folds the serialized operation text into the digest and threads the schema string through the visitor"
  lang rust
  file apollo-router/src/spec/query/change.rs
  reject VYQL-CRY-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-036
  reject VYQL-AUTH-058
  code
  ```
  impl<'a> QueryHashVisitor<'a> {
      pub(crate) fn hash_query(
          schema: &'a schema::Schema,
          schema_str: &'a str,
          executable: &'a executable::ExecutableDocument,
          operation_name: Option<&str>,
      ) -> Result<Vec<u8>, BoxError> {
          let mut visitor = QueryHashVisitor::new(schema, schema_str, executable);
          traverse::document(&mut visitor, executable, operation_name)?;
          executable.to_string().hash(&mut visitor);
          Ok(visitor.finish())
      }

      pub(crate) fn finish(self) -> Vec<u8> {
          self.hasher.finalize().as_slice().into()
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1687: the visitor's field hook hashes parent type, name and arguments only, so an introspection field carries none of the schema it answers from"
  lang rust
  file apollo-router/src/spec/query/change.rs
  reject VYQL-CRY-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-036
  code
  ```
  impl<'a> Visitor for QueryHashVisitor<'a> {
      fn field(
          &mut self,
          parent_type: &str,
          field_def: &ast::FieldDefinition,
          node: &executable::Field,
      ) -> Result<(), BoxError> {
          self.hash_field(
              parent_type.to_string(),
              field_def.name.as_str().to_string(),
              field_def,
              &node.arguments,
          )?;

          traverse::field(self, field_def, node)
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1687: the fixed revision folds the whole schema string into the digest when the visitor meets an introspection field"
  lang rust
  file apollo-router/src/spec/query/change.rs
  reject VYQL-CRY-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-036
  code
  ```
  impl<'a> Visitor for QueryHashVisitor<'a> {
      fn field(
          &mut self,
          parent_type: &str,
          field_def: &ast::FieldDefinition,
          node: &executable::Field,
      ) -> Result<(), BoxError> {
          if !self.seen_introspection && (field_def.name == "__schema" || field_def.name == "__type")
          {
              self.seen_introspection = true;
              self.schema_str.hash(self);
          }

          self.hash_field(
              parent_type.to_string(),
              field_def.name.as_str().to_string(),
              field_def,
              &node.arguments,
          )?;

          traverse::field(self, field_def, node)
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1687: the distributed plan-cache key mixes the projection hash, operation name, metadata and plan options but not the operation text or the schema"
  lang rust
  file apollo-router/src/query_planner/caching_query_planner.rs
  reject VYQL-CRY-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-036
  reject VYQL-AUTH-058
  code
  ```
  #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
  pub(crate) struct CachingQueryKey {
      pub(crate) query: String,
      pub(crate) operation: Option<String>,
      pub(crate) hash: Arc<QueryHash>,
      pub(crate) metadata: CacheKeyMetadata,
      pub(crate) plan_options: PlanOptions,
  }

  impl std::fmt::Display for CachingQueryKey {
      fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> std::fmt::Result {
          let mut hasher = Sha256::new();
          hasher.update(self.operation.as_deref().unwrap_or("-"));
          let operation = hex::encode(hasher.finalize());

          let mut hasher = Sha256::new();
          hasher.update(&serde_json::to_vec(&self.metadata).expect("serialization should not fail"));
          hasher.update(
              &serde_json::to_vec(&self.plan_options).expect("serialization should not fail"),
          );
          let metadata = hex::encode(hasher.finalize());

          write!(
              f,
              "plan:{}:{}:{}:{}",
              FEDERATION_VERSION, self.hash, operation, metadata,
          )
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1687: the fixed revision adds the raw schema SDL to the distributed plan-cache key"
  lang rust
  file apollo-router/src/query_planner/caching_query_planner.rs
  reject VYQL-CRY-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-036
  reject VYQL-AUTH-058
  code
  ```
  #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
  pub(crate) struct CachingQueryKey {
      pub(crate) query: String,
      pub(crate) sdl: Arc<String>,
      pub(crate) operation: Option<String>,
      pub(crate) hash: Arc<QueryHash>,
      pub(crate) metadata: CacheKeyMetadata,
      pub(crate) plan_options: PlanOptions,
  }

  impl std::fmt::Display for CachingQueryKey {
      fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> std::fmt::Result {
          let mut hasher = Sha256::new();
          hasher.update(self.operation.as_deref().unwrap_or("-"));
          let operation = hex::encode(hasher.finalize());

          let mut hasher = Sha256::new();
          hasher.update(&serde_json::to_vec(&self.metadata).expect("serialization should not fail"));
          hasher.update(
              &serde_json::to_vec(&self.plan_options).expect("serialization should not fail"),
          );
          hasher.update(&serde_json::to_vec(&self.sdl).expect("serialization should not fail"));
          let metadata = hex::encode(hasher.finalize());

          write!(
              f,
              "plan:{}:{}:{}:{}",
              FEDERATION_VERSION, self.hash, operation, metadata,
          )
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1687: the only hash-shaped finding in the file is the weak-algorithm one on the stats-report key, unchanged by the fix"
  lang rust
  file apollo-router/src/query_planner/caching_query_planner.rs
  expect VYQL-CRY-001
  code
  ```
  fn stats_report_key_hash(stats_report_key: &str) -> String {
      let mut hasher = sha1::Sha1::new();
      hasher.update(stats_report_key.as_bytes());
      let result = hasher.finalize();
      hex::encode(result)
  }
  ```
